docker tag <source> <dest> => To tag an image with a second tag
docker inspect <imageid> => to see details about an image
docker inspect <containerid> => to see details about a container
docker logs <containerid> => to see logs of a container
docker logs -f <containerid> => to see logs and keep logs appearing
docker run -p <hostport>:<containerport> <image> => to publish a port 


lsblk => to see disks and partition details
blkid => to see UUID and fs of a disk or partition 

mkfs.<fstype>  => to create a file system on a disk or a partition 
   1. xfs
   2. ext4
   3. ext3

mount <devname> <mountpoint> => to mount a disk to a mount 
  a. doesn't persist over reboot 

to make the mount persistent => use /etc/fstab
then mount -a


gdisk <diskname> => to create a gpt partition on a disk
then 
  a. ? for help
  b. n for new partition 
  c. w write the part table and exit

fdisk <diskname> => to create a partiotion on a disk  
